## 5. Low-band theorem, zero modes, and limits

For signed momentum integers \(|n_\mu|\le L/2\),
\(\sin(\pi|n_\mu|/L)\ge2|n_\mu|/L\), hence \(\Omega\ge4|n|/L\).
A nonempty hard band \(0<\Omega\le\epsilon\), \(0<\epsilon\le2\),
has \(L\epsilon\ge4\). With \(R=L\epsilon/4\ge1\),

\[
N_\epsilon\le(2\lfloor R\rfloor+1)^3\le27R^3,\qquad
N_\epsilon/V\le27\epsilon^3/64.
\]

The zero mode is excluded; overcounting boundary momentum representatives
only enlarges this upper bound. For one plaquette the full transverse
polarization sum is \((D_\mu+D_\nu)/D\le1\), so
\(\sum_{\rm band}d_{pr}^2/\Omega_r\le27\epsilon^3/128\).
Weighted Cauchy with weight \(\mu\), followed by the triangle inequality
on an exact filling, gives
\(|\chi_z|^2\le\mu\ell_z^2(27/128)\epsilon^3\).
At a link, the diagonal of the transverse rank-two projector is at most
1 per nonzero momentum; there is no additional polarization factor two.
Thus \(|\xi_e|^2\le\mu(27/128)\epsilon^3\).

The magnetic weight \(436/4=109\) and electric weight 24 yield exactly

\[
\left(1-\frac{3591}{128}\epsilon^3\right)\frac{\mu}{\tau}
\le\lim_{g\downarrow0}\Delta_g\le\frac{\mu}{\tau}.
\]

This is a sufficient bound. The PRE's cubic-symmetric projector trace
gave the sharper count-dependent loss \((133/3)N_L(\Lambda)/V\), with
its own energy-tail and fixed-gap qualifications. Different strength does
not make the root bound wrong.

